.Dd October 29, 2026
.Dt DYNAMIC_PAGER 8
.Os Minkar
.Sh NAME
.Nm dynamic_pager
.Nd set where the swap files go
.Sh SYNOPSIS
.Nm
.Op Fl F Ar filename
.Op Fl S Ar filesize
.Op Fl H Ar high-water-trigger
.Op Fl L Ar low-water-trigger
.Sh DESCRIPTION
The kernel's memory compressor writes the pages it cannot keep in memory to
swap files, which it creates, grows and removes itself.
.Nm
tells it where they go: the path
.Ar filename
followed by a number
.Pq Pa swapfile0 , Pa swapfile1 , No ...
\&.
It creates the directory if it does not exist, sets the prefix and exits.
.Bl -tag -width indent
.It Fl F Ar filename
The prefix of the swap files' paths; by default
.Pa /private/var/vm/swapfile .
.It Fl S , Fl H , Fl L
Sizes and triggers that older versions used; accepted and ignored.
.El
.Pp
The prefix in use is the
.Va vm.swapfileprefix
sysctl; how much swap is used is
.Va vm.swapusage .
.Sh FILES
.Bl -tag -width indent
.It Pa /private/var/vm/swapfile*
the swap files
.El
.Sh EXIT STATUS
.Ex -std
.Sh SEE ALSO
.Xr sysctl 8 ,
.Xr vm_stat 1
